  "question": {
    "text": "An engine pumps water continuously through a hose. Water leaves the hose with velocity $v$ and $m$ is mass per unit length of the water jet. If this jet hits a surface and came to rest instantaneously, the force on the surface is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "ceNIt",
      "text": "\n$m v^3$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "nv10d",
      "text": "\n$m v^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "O0lsY",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} m v^2$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "d8ySN",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{2} m v^3$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "As power $\\mathrm{P}=F . v .=\\frac{F \\ell}{t}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\text { or, } v\\left(M \\frac{v}{t}\\right)=\\frac{F . \\ell}{t} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad M v^2=F \\ell \\ell \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\quad F=\\frac{M}{\\ell} v^2=m v^2 \\\\\n& {\\left[\\because \\frac{M}{\\ell}=m(\\text { given })\\right]}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
